  "description": "Drowned in overwhelming guilt and despair, Father Vence Reich decides to end it all in the quiet solitude of his village monastery. But just as his fingers brace on the trigger of his rifle, a blinding white light bursts through the gloom. Suspended from the attic ceiling is a terrifying yet mesmerizing entity—and Vence instantly falls to his knees, convinced he is looking at God. As he surrenders both his body and soul to this \"God\" of snake-like tongues and luminous tentacles, Vence spirals into a deep, consuming dependency. In the name of devotion, the unholy communion begins... \n\n(Source: Lezhin US)\n\n*Note: Includes six extra chapters.*",
